From 8e3292f0603518841743e6b2cbd4e5386d6aa6b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac125b <mac125b@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:38:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] native Windows: fused HC mix (GGML_OP_HC_MIX), online
 stop-rule verify times, CPU help for MoE cache misses (opt-in), MTP head
 sharing (opt-in)

- GGML_OP_HC_MIX: the hyper-connection mix (per-stream RMS norm, inject, down, SiLU, up, gated mean) as one op for <= 8 tokens:
  CUDA hc-mix.cu (rms, down+inject, up+pre kernels), CPU reference; qwen4exp uses it for the layer mixers (LLAMA_HC_MIX_FUSED=0 off).
  All-hit verify of 4 tokens on an RTX 4090: 17.66 -> 15.91 ms.
- stop rule (LLAMA_SPEC_STOP): verify time by width learned online from the measured rounds (EMA, monotone in the width, one
  round moves it by -40/+50 % at most) and one overruled stop every 16 rounds to keep measuring the next width
  (LLAMA_SPEC_STOP_ONLINE, LLAMA_SPEC_STOP_EXPLORE).
- MoE cache CPU help (LLAMA_MOE_CPU=1, off by default): GGML_OP_MOE_FETCH leaves capped single-token misses to a CPU worker
  (all-zero slot on the GPU, MoE input and jobs in a page-locked box, bell without CUDA sync), GGML_OP_MOE_CPU_RECV adds the CPU
  rows; admission of CPU misses by DMA on a second stream; tuning env vars (threads, affinity, jobs, max tokens, admit), VERIFY /
  NOOP / DEBUG switches and GPU-side window/wait timing. Not faster than the GPU-only lookup yet on this PC.
- MTP: llama_model_share_output (LLAMA_MTP_SHARE_HEAD=1) lets the draft use the target's head; the coarse draft head is placed on
  the GPU when the real head is in host memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
